cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Code for the object-detection model in "Top Down or Bottom Up? Evidence
  from a Field Experiment on Public Goods Provision"
message: If you use this code, please cite the paper.
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Coccia
    given-names: Carla
    affiliation: University of Bern
    email: carla.coccia@unibe.ch
  - family-names: Jakob
    given-names: Martina
    affiliation: University of Zurich
    email: martina.jakob@econ.uzh.ch

abstract: >-
  Training and evaluation code for the YOLO26 object-detection model that
  measures street contamination in "Top Down or Bottom Up? Evidence from a Field
  Experiment on Public Goods Provision". The model is fine-tuned on geotagged
  street photographs from the MICOLI field experiment in 120 rural communities in
  Morazan, El Salvador, together with the public TACO, extended TACO and
  Plastopol trash datasets. Its per-photograph trash counts are the paper's
  measure of street contamination.

keywords:
  - object detection
  - YOLO
  - deep learning
  - solid waste management
  - randomized controlled trial
  - El Salvador

license: AGPL-3.0
repository-code: https://github.com/carlaalessandracoccia/yolo-waste-detection
